cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or data, please cite it using the metadata from this file, and cite the accompanying article."
type: software
title: "Hummell-2026: analysis code for 'Receptor-proximal phosphoform organization precedes β2 integrin activation'"
abstract: >-
  Python statistical engine and processed TMTpro 18-plex quantification tables
  for APEX2 proximity labeling of the β2 integrin CD18 (ITGB2) against a
  compartment-matched CAAX-APEX2 membrane reference in Jurkat T cells under
  resting (BSA), ICAM-1 and ICAM-1 plus PMA conditions. Implements median
  loading normalization, a day-blocked cell-means design with sample quality
  weights, limma-trend empirical Bayes moderated t statistics, equivalence
  testing by two one-sided tests, the phosphosite selectivity index (PSI) and
  difference-of-differences contrasts for receptor-preferential activation
  responses. Raw mass spectrometry data are deposited in PRIDE (PXD085432).
